    "turn_text": "But her father was a career army officer and was an army colonel. So I was a Navy Ensign proposing to the army colonel's daughter. So Stephanie is now ranked me for 32 years. And, you know, her father served in Vietnam for two tours. He was at the Battle of Quezon in 1968 during the Tet Offensive, the worst place literally on the planet to be in 1968 here in three bronze stars with combat V. And as a young girl, Stephanie, her father was stationed in Germany and Stephanie remembers the alerts in the middle of the night and all the soldiers and her dad put his combat boots and running out the door and not seeing him for four or five days and not knowing. you know, what was going on because they were right at the place where they expected the Soviet Union to come into Western Europe. And so there is a sense of identity around protecting the nation, about serving the nation that resonates with her and it resonated with me. Congress is very much like that, and I think my sense of calling to run for this office and to serve this community comes from that same place. And getting back to people that make a decision to start a small farm, which we've done, or to open up a restaurant, thankfully we've not done that, although my wife is great in hospitality. Don't do it.",
