  {
    "episode_id": 78358,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78358.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 39,
    "turn_text": "I can't imagine it feels like such a daunting thing to become a congressman, to step into that role in that position. Having never come from politics or being in a government position before, to them walking into that, going through the campaign process, which I'd imagine, just from this current campaign, is we get, for some reason, I don't know why. My wife is a registered Democrat. I get all of her texts, all of her political texts and calls. I get hello to my cell phone, hello, Rebecca. We hope that you can join us in joining the campaign for Kamala Harris or for John Mann, or anything. You were a modern man. Yeah, all right. And anyways, but just getting all of the mailers from every level of the campaign, every office right now, it is, Wild to me how ugly some of them can get. I mean, I just got one or anti Caleb Slater Flyer in the mail and I just remember it was just this terrible terrible picture of him and I just thought to myself, imagine running for office thinking you're in a, you hope that you get elected, you can make a difference. And then one day in the mail that shows up, someone who's taken this thing and just completely, you know, made you out to be the worst person imaginable. I can't imagine dealing with just that.",
