  {
    "episode_id": 78358,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78358.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 40,
    "turn_text": "Let me tell you two anecdotes on that to make that personal. First is when Stephanie and I go out on a date, which is not very often these days, unfortunately, we have to find a place that doesn't have televisions because we can't sit there. and have these horrible ads come up and say these horrible and frankly, untrue things about us while we're sitting there trying to have a nice meal. We take that with a grain of salt, it just comes with the territory. The second thing is I have 500 days at sea on a nuclear submarine. With 160 guys, I may or may not have liked a whole lot. And the culture on a submarine is your misery is our entertainment. And so for 80 days straight, you know, I'll have people poke at you trying to find what gets under your skin. And as soon as they find something, the whole crew knows and everybody's in on it. And so, you know, when I get trolled, which I often do by different people on politics, I just look at them and I smile and I think you're an amateur. You have no idea",
