    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78358.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 47,
    "turn_text": "We do. So that's what brought us here 15 years ago is we have family in the area and we moved to be close to family and to start this farm. And the farm came out of a, And your readers and your listeners will really connect with this because you travel to places like France or New Zealand and you see farm to table and you just think about what it would be like to be part of that. So we did a lot of research. Stephanie and I did a lot of research. And there's some experimental methods for cultivating burgundy truffles and different kinds of truffles on the roots of hazelnut trees. And we looked at vineyards, and vineyards require a lot of money. They require a lot of care and maintenance. And we felt like we weren't going to be able to put that in. We were looking for something that we could establish. cook, you know, maintain.",
